      * p, an *note integer: (Macaulay2Doc)ZZ,, prime characteristic of the
        field
      * L, a *note list: (Macaulay2Doc)List,, list of integers $a_1,...,a_n$
  * *note Optional inputs: (Macaulay2Doc)using functions with optional inputs,:
      * *note UseConjecture: UseConjecture, => ..., default value false, An
        option that, whenever the Han-Monsky is computed, allows the user to
        choose if employ Conjecture 4.1 [KMRR,25] or not
  * Outputs:
      * a *note Boolean value: (Macaulay2Doc)Boolean,, whether the monomial
        complete intersections $A=k[x_1,...,x_n]/(x_1^{a_1}, …, x_n^{a_n})$,
        where k is a field of characteristic p, has the Strong Lefschetz
        property.

Description
===========

Check if the monomial complete intersections $A=k[x_1,...,x_n]/(x_1^{a_1}, …,
x_n^{a_n})$, where k is a field of characteristic p has the Strong Lefschetz
property using Theorem 3.4 of [Nicklasson,18].

